      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "question"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "It is given that AB || CD and CD || EF. Therefore, AB || CD || EF (Lines parallel to the same line are parallel to each other). It can be observed that x = z (Alternate interior angles). It is given that y: z = 3: 7. Let the common ratio between y and z be a. y = 3a and z = 7a. Also, x + y = 180º (Co-interior angles on the same side of the transversal). Therefore, z + y = 180º. 7a + 3a = 180º. 10a = 180º, a = 18º. Thus, x = 7a = 7 × 18º = 126º.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [
      {
        "step_number": 1,
        "description": "Establish that AB || CD and CD || EF implies AB || CD || EF.",
        "expression": null
      },
